WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:05.310
The prepared row still has the same
forty five ordered calendar values.

00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:07.930
We have not rebuilt the
dataset for this model.

00:00:08.540 --> 00:00:12.770
The helper checks that one of the first
twenty four hour positions is active.

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:15.820
It also reads the named working day flag.

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:21.010
For the Monday eight o'clock row,
those selected values form eight, one.

00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:24.970
The model does not use month or
the separate weekday columns.

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:29.900
Its receipt records the twenty four
encoded hour columns and the working day

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:31.530
column as used inputs.

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:33.310
The target stays separate.

00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:36.690
Extracting this key
interprets a fixed schema;

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:39.850
it does not learn a transform
from validation data.

00:00:42.202 --> 00:00:46.472
Fitting first calculates the global
training mean for the fallback.

00:00:46.962 --> 00:00:50.392
The loop then visits paired
training keys and targets.

00:00:51.062 --> 00:00:54.652
Strict pairing prevents silently
dropping an unmatched value.

00:00:55.302 --> 00:00:59.612
Each key is validated before its target
is appended to that group's list.

00:01:00.282 --> 00:01:02.052
For eight, one,

00:01:02.182 --> 00:01:06.672
the completed list contains two hundred
and forty eight observed targets.

00:01:07.262 --> 00:01:09.952
Their sum is eighty six thousand,
six hundred and seventy seven.

00:01:11.622 --> 00:01:13.972
No validation rows enter this loop.

00:01:14.462 --> 00:01:17.432
A group retains its mean
and its support count,

00:01:17.662 --> 00:01:21.632
while the model retains the fallback
and its full training count.

00:01:22.062 --> 00:01:25.772
These saved statistics are enough
to repeat the prediction later.

00:01:27.942 --> 00:01:30.852
Why use a mean inside each group?

00:01:31.362 --> 00:01:35.232
Take the same half squared error
used for the global constant,

00:01:35.362 --> 00:01:38.112
now restricted to one
group's training rows.

00:01:38.642 --> 00:01:43.172
Its derivative is the chosen constant
minus that group's average target.

00:01:43.902 --> 00:01:46.672
Setting the derivative to
zero gives the group mean.

00:01:47.162 --> 00:01:50.112
We solve this separately
for every observed group.

00:01:50.622 --> 00:01:52.652
These values are fitted parameters,

00:01:53.082 --> 00:01:56.832
even though we obtain them by
arithmetic rather than gradient descent.

00:01:57.422 --> 00:01:59.992
More groups permit a richer function.

00:02:00.482 --> 00:02:02.572
This objective is squared error.

00:02:03.062 --> 00:02:07.642
A reporting preference for mean absolute
error does not make the fitted means into

00:02:07.642 --> 00:02:10.832
medians or guarantee the
best validation score.

00:02:13.022 --> 00:02:16.492
Prediction builds a lookup from
the saved group statistics.

00:02:17.322 --> 00:02:21.372
It validates each requested key
and returns its fitted value,

00:02:21.502 --> 00:02:25.392
using the saved global fallback
when the valid key is absent.

00:02:25.882 --> 00:02:30.272
For eight, one, it returns three
hundred and forty nine point five zero.

00:02:30.962 --> 00:02:33.972
The method never receives the later
target of four hundred and twenty.

00:02:35.062 --> 00:02:38.772
Repeating a call does not change
a mean or increment a count.

00:02:39.262 --> 00:02:41.932
The runner attaches each
result to its record,

00:02:42.262 --> 00:02:44.832
target time and issue time before scoring.

00:02:45.462 --> 00:02:48.012
The parameters stay frozen
throughout validation.

00:02:48.742 --> 00:02:52.402
Updating them from validation answers
would define a different evaluation

00:02:52.402 --> 00:02:53.172
protocol.

00:02:55.400 --> 00:02:59.510
A small integration fixture
tests that separation directly.

00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:05.140
Its training data stays fixed while
validation targets change from sixteen to

00:03:05.140 --> 00:03:06.030
one thousand.

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:11.190
Both runs produce identical fitted
group statistics and the same fallback.

00:03:11.660 --> 00:03:16.070
Their validation mean absolute errors
change from nine to nine hundred and

00:03:16.070 --> 00:03:16.910
seventy five.

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:20.790
The outcome change affects scoring,
where it belongs.

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:26.290
The fixture also runs after its raw
file and test export have been removed.

00:03:26.900 --> 00:03:28.810
Thirty eight code checks pass,

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:33.030
and the real predictions have separate
arithmetic and identity verification.

00:03:34.040 --> 00:03:36.750
These checks establish
implementation behavior.

00:03:37.420 --> 00:03:41.180
The learner's explanation and the
later modelling handoff remain separate

00:03:41.180 --> 00:03:41.770
evidence.

